FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] tests/unreviewed_work_ack_test.rs:201 — The phase acknowledges its own delivery commit by pinning the SHA `653c3d34...`, but the pipeline re-creates the phase’s delivery commit every round. When the uncommitted changes are committed, `HEAD` gets a new SHA; `edge_the_phase_under_review_acknowledges_its_delivery_by_reviewed_sha_not_a_self_prefix` reads `HEAD` fresh at `:1958` and requires that SHA in `ACKNOWLEDGED` at `:1975`, while the fixed entry at `:201` is either stale or the new delivery commit is unacknowledged. The file itself documents this failure mode at `:70-79`: a SHA-pinned delivery commit goes stale when rebuilt. — Concrete fix: do not write the phase’s own delivery SHA into the working tree; have the pipeline append the final SHA after delivery, or acknowledge the phase-under-review delivery by a pipeline-owned rule rather than a SHA the phase writes. Remove the `653c...` entry and the `HEAD`-SHA assertion until the delivery SHA is stable. — VERIFIED: traced `:1958-1979` (fresh `git log -1 HEAD`, then `ACKNOWLEDGED.iter().any(|entry| *entry == sha)`) against the fixed SHA at `:201`, plus the stale check at `:987-992`.

2. [MAJOR] tests/bench_test.rs:1419 — `edge_cli_named_workload_uses_its_default_size` never asserts the size actually used. It computes `expected` at `:1424` but only uses it in an assertion message at `:1428`; the assertions at `:1425-1437` check exit code and absence of writes. A regression where `run_cli` ignores `default_size` and runs size `0` for every workload would still pass this test. — Concrete fix: capture the emitted table (or expose the resolved `(name, size)` from the CLI path) and assert the rendered row contains `default_size(name)`, not merely that the command exited zero.

3. [MINOR] tests/bench/mod.rs:902 — `truncate` counts Unicode scalar values, not terminal display width, so a 20-character CJK answer occupies about 40 columns and breaks the aligned table. `tests/bench_test.rs:1211` reinforces the wrong model by calling 20 CJK characters the “full 20-character column width.” — Concrete fix: pad/truncate by display width (e.g. `unicode-width`) or explicitly document and test character-count truncation without claiming column alignment.

